This repository incorporates or adapts code from these projects, under
the terms noted:

- hmans/beans (Apache-2.0): the fractional-order algorithm in
  packages/tasks/src/fractional.ts is a port of pkg/bean/fractional.go, and
  the task files in packages/tasks/fixtures/beans-corpus/ are copies of
  files from its .beans/ directory, used as test data. Apache-2.0 code may
  be included in GPL-3 works; this NOTICE records the origin and the
  license.
- zhaono1/agent-playbook (MIT): the lesson lifecycle states, the start
  packet and the eval-artifact contract in packages/hooks/src/lessons/,
  and the host-conformance states in packages/adapters/src/conformance.ts,
  are adapted from its self-improving-agent, eval-artifact and
  long-task-coordinator designs.
- miqdadbadjuber/anti-slop (MIT): the quality rules in packages/quality/
  are adapted from its rules, keeping the R-XX identifiers in rule
  metadata. The skills in templates/.opencode/skills/ adapt the same
  upstream rules: oa-ui carries the purpose test, oa-copy the
  anti-slop-copywriting rules, and oa-comments the anti-slop-code tells
  and their preserve list.
- Nutlope/hallmark (MIT): the floor rules and the tier system in
  packages/quality/ are adapted from its rules, keeping the Floor numbers.
  The material inventory in templates/.opencode/skills/oa-ui/ is adapted
  from its rules as well. Its sloplint.mjs is called as an external check
  when installed, not vendored: the bridge in packages/quality/src/sloplint.ts
  looks for it, runs it over the pages and the stylesheets of the change,
  and keeps the static findings when it is not there. The linter is
  optional, and none of it is bundled. The license of the scripts is not
  stated here, because it has not been read: it is unknown, and it needs a
  check against an installed copy of the linter.
- junhoyeo/tokscale (MIT) and xiufengsun/TokenTracker (MIT): ideas only —
  OpenCode database discovery, the pricing fallback chain, the outcomes
  sidecar and the privacy rule. No code copied.
- EcoLogits (CC BY-SA 4.0, docs): the footprint formulas in
  packages/footprint/ are re-implemented from the published methodology,
  https://github.com/mlco2/ecologits, with credit in the UI and this NOTICE.
  Its models.json data is fetched at runtime and cached, not bundled, until
  its data license is confirmed.
- models.dev (MIT): model and cost data, bundled at build time through
  the @opencode-ai/models package.
